BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fresh Cheesemaking with Botanical Flavors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T180000
UID:261022rlAmHHC_HUidr8M6epKBRg
DESCRIPTION:Fresh cheese is one of the most approachable and rewarding thi
 ngs to make at home. In Sonoma County’s rich dairy landscape\, these sim
 ple cheeses have long been a staple—equally at home in everyday meals an
 d on a shared table.\n\nIn this hands-on workshop\, you’ll learn how to 
 make fresh cheeses from cow and goat milk\, while exploring how herbs\, fl
 owers\, and citrus can shape flavor in simple\, elegant ways. We’ll cove
 r the essential techniques behind fresh cheesemaking so you can confidentl
 y recreate them in your own kitchen.\n\nIn this workshop you’ll:\n\n• 
 Learn the fundamentals of fresh cheesemaking using cow and goat milk\n\n
 • Understand key concepts in cheesemaking\, including acidity\, texture
 \, and food safety\n\n• Make goat milk chèvre with edible flowers and w
 ith rosemary and honey\n\n• Prepare fresh ricotta with Meyer lemon\n\n
 • Explore how to incorporate herbs\, flowers\, and other botanicals int
 o your cheeses\n\nYou’ll work alongside instructor Willow\, a Sonoma Cou
 nty farmer and educator\, whose approach connects practical kitchen skills
  with a deeper understanding of ingredients and process.\n\nYou’ll leave
  with recipes\, techniques\, and the confidence to begin making fresh chee
 se at home.\n\nNo prior cheesemaking experience required.
LOCATION:Gather Sebastopol
URL:https://gathersebastopol.com/products/fresh-cheesemaking-with-botanica
 l-flavors
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Art of Broom Making
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T130000
UID:261022ofWmiw3Gdk-1TucWvSR7Jg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a hands-on workshop where tradition meets artistry
 . Alissa Kaplan\, maker and founder of Zizland Atelier\, will guide you th
 rough the craft of broom making as you create your own Wrapped Hawk Tail W
 hisk—a beautiful and functional hand broom with deep roots in American f
 olk tradition.\n\nIn this 3-hour class\, you’ll learn:\n\n• A brief hi
 story and uses of hand brooms\n\n• Traditional Shaker/Appalachian bindin
 g and wrapping techniques\n\n• How to select and prepare broomcorn for a
  whisk\n\n• Step-by-step guidance to craft your own wrapped Hawk Tail Wh
 isk to take home\n\nWhether you’re drawn to heritage crafts\, seasonal r
 ituals\, or simply love working with your hands\, this workshop offers a m
 eaningful way to connect with timeless skills and leave with something use
 ful and beautiful.\n\nSome hand strength is required. Material and tools w
 ill be supplied.
LOCATION:Gather Sebastopol
URL:https://gathersebastopol.com/products/the-art-of-broom-making
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Familias al aire libre en la Reserva de Fairfield Osborn
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T160000
UID:261022jpGTJj7CHkuI1ZfU8zKjeg
DESCRIPTION:En español:\n\nAcompañé a Sonoma  Land Trust y el Centro 
 de Investigación Medioambiental de la Universidad de Sonoma State para el
  paseo mensual llamado Familias al Aire Libre. Estos paseos son dirigidos 
 en español\, hay transportación disponible\, son gratuitos\, y diseñado
 s con actividades para toda la familia – padres\, abuelitos\, hijos e hi
 jas chicos y grandes – y ocurren cada cuarto sábado del mes. Las 450 ac
 res de la reserva Fairfield Osborn sirven como centro de educación e inve
 stigación medioambiental. ¡Ven a descubrir su importancia ecológica y c
 ómo puedes participar más en la reserva!\n\nEnglish Translation:\n\nJoin
  Sonoma Land Trust and Sonoma State’s Center for Environmental Inquiry
  for a bilingual family outing at Fairfield Osborn Preserve. SLT’s month
 ly  Familias al Aire Libre outings are free\, Spanish-forward\, 
 transportation is made available\, and are designed with activities 
 for the whole family – parents\, grandparents\, young children\, and
  teens. Fairfield Osborn Preserve’s 450 acres serve as a center 
 for environmental education and inquiry. Come learn about its ecologic
 al importance and how you can get further involved with the preserve!
LOCATION:Fairfield Osborn Preserve
URL:https://cei.sonoma.edu/Familias-al-aire-libre-en-la-Reserva-de-Fairfie
 ld-Osborn
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
