 w and Something Familiar"... Roots Rock\, Americana\, Country Blues\, West
 ern Swing\, Cajun\, and New Orleans music...\n\nno cover\, Tip the perform
 ers! $10+ donation suggested\n\nHattie Craven 2:30-4:00\n\nHattie Craven h
 as lived and breathed music since her early years with her father\, award-
 winning performer Joe Craven. Hattie draws musical influences from Amy Win
 ehouse\, Joni Mitchell\, James Brown\, Louis Prima\, and so many more. She
  effectively reimagines traditional folk\, bluegrass\, country\, jazz and 
 pop\,\n\ncreating new music that is truly her own. Hattie is also a fine w
 riter of original songs that explore themes of love\, loss and resilience.
  https://www.hattiecraven.com\n\nBack pOrchEstra: 4:45-6:45\n\nSemi-Acoust
 ic Original Indie Rock & the American Roots\n\nthat inspired it: Country B
 lues\, Cajun\, Roots Rock\,\n\nAmericana\, Singer/Songwriter music with ri
 ch tones:\n\nCandy Girard\, Tim Eschliman\, Mark Larson\, Jen Rund\, Luis 
 Rodriguez... originals and reworked classics by Hank Williams\, Taj Mahal\
