DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T120000
UID:260312ev42Vb98HkKjn-qi-wCM3A
DESCRIPTION:The Healdsburg Certified Farmers Markets began in 1978\, and i
 s one of the original 22 markets to open in the state that year. Featuring
  an abundance of produce and flowers grown in the region\, as well as inno
 vative food products\, delicious foods to eat on site\, and a variety of c
 reative crafts\, this farmers market shines as an example of the diverse a
 nd delicious offerings of this area.
LOCATION:Foley Family Community Pavilion
URL:https://www.healdsburgfarmersmarket.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T094500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T101500
UID:2602124z-FkW0LZE2gzyW6X0fMhQ
DESCRIPTION:Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.\n\nOvereaters An
 onymous \\(OA\\) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits. \n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on first
 \, second and fourth Saturdays of the month from 9:45 - 10:15 AM at ​Uni
 tarian Universalist Congregation of Marin\, 240 Channing Way\, San Rafael 
 CA 94903. Contact: Sue M. 415-298-6792​. You may view all North Bay OA 
 in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html\
 n\nIn OA\, members experience spiritual\, emotional\, and physical recover
 y by practicing the Twelve Steps and living by their spiritual principles
 —one day at a time.\n\nOA is not a diet club or calorie-counting program
 .\n\nMembers have different plans of eating.\n\nOA does not endorse any sp
 ecific food plan. \n\nIf food is causing problems in your life\, you don
 ’t have to struggle alone. Recovery is possible\, and help is available.
 \n\nVisit: https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\nFind a meeting: https://www.nort
 hbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Unitarian Universalist Congregation of Marin
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pumpkins on Pikes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T140000
UID:261023rcT6VEBM90OhguLiJnivCg
DESCRIPTION:In addition to producing healthy and sustainable local food\, 
 Petaluma's  Tara Firma Farms also puts on fantastic family-friendly events
  throughout the year. Come on out to the farm for Halloween fun with pumpk
 in carving\, live music\, a straw maze\, games\, food\, drinks\, and more.
  Pumpkins on Pikes takes place on Saturday\, October 17 and 24 and Sunday\
 , October 25\, from 2 to 9 pm. The festivities start in the afternoon with
  great food\, live music and pumpkin carving. Everyone will get the chance
  to display their Jack-O-Lantern on a pike in the corn field. When the sun
  goes down the pumpkins are lit. It is a truly heart warming feeling looki
 ng over the glowing corn field to see the individual creations of all who 
 attend. Free pumpkins for carving will be provided with admission. Bring y
 our pumpkin carving tools\, blankets and coats to stay warm after dark\, a
 nd a sheet to cover hay bales for seating. Admission is $40 and includes a
  carving pumpkin. Children 3 and under are admitted free \\(no pumpkin pro
 vided\\). Tickets must be ordered in advance and are not available at the 
 door.
LOCATION:Tara Firma Farms 3796 I St
URL:https://www.marinmommies.com/calendar/pumpkins-pikes-0
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annual Cemetery Tour 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T123000
UID:261023hcyFFDNmUkq4AsN2aPvQew
DESCRIPTION:Ghosts of Petaluma’s Past Come to Life on Our Annual Cemeter
 y Tour! \n\n27th ANNUAL CEMETERY WALK PRESENTED BY THE PETALUMANS OF YESTE
 RYEAR\n\nSaturday\, October 24\, 2026 – Starting times: 10:30 a.m. and 1
 1:00 am\n\nTicket Cost:  $20 \n\nCypress Hill Cemetery\n\n430 Magnolia A
 ve\, Petaluma CA\n\nGo to EventBrite for Tickets \n\nJoin the Petalumans o
 f Yesteryear for a guided graveside tour featuring some of the most notabl
 e and interesting residents of early Petaluma. \n\nYou’ll hear colorful 
 stories about life \\(and death\\) in our town’s early days\, directly f
 rom our costumed living history docents representing the likes of Lyman By
 ce\, Addie Atwater\, Ida Belle McNear\, and many others. \n\nThe tour begi
 ns at the Cypress Hill Memorial Park office parking lot and concludes insi
 de the Cypress Hill columbarium\, which was designed by noted Petaluma arc
 hitect Brainerd Jones. Wear comfortable shoes. Please note: Do not contact
  the cemetery regarding this tour. Contact the Petaluma Historical Library
  & Museum with any questions at 707-778-4398. \n\nPlease check-in on arriv
 al – we will have your name on the door list. \n\nGo to EventBrite for T
 ickets
LOCATION:Cypress Hill Cemetery
URL:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/annual-cemetery-tour-202
 6/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
