BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Poet Jeremy Raikes's book signing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T180000
UID:2610217_Wk7JuXEkix13DFXTWsNw
DESCRIPTION:Poet Jeremy Raikes \\(well known to many in Sonoma County as t
 he Chair Repair Guy!\\) will celebrate his 90th birthday and the publicati
 on of his poetry collection\, Delicious Suspicions\, with a book signing 
 and birthday gathering on Sunday\, October 25\, 2026\, at 4:00 p.m. at Won
 derland Pizzeria\, 20391 Highway 116 in Monte Rio.\n\nRaised on a cattle r
 anch in Argentina by expat British parents\, in the 1960's Jeremy was an a
 dvertising writer at J Walter Thompson \\(then the largest advertising age
 ncy in the world\\) and later became creative director of their Mexico Cit
 y office. While at Thompson\, Jeremy collaborated with Charles Schultz on 
 a series of animated Peanuts ads for the Ford Motor Company.\n\nThe occasi
 on offers readers a chance to meet Jeremy\, purchase a signed copy of his 
 book and celebrate a writer whose work approaches life with humor\, tender
 ness and an enduring sense of wonder.\n\nDelicious Suspicions explores lo
 ve\, friendship\, loss\, aging and the pleasures of everyday encounters. P
 layful wordplay and conversational rhythms sit alongside candid reflection
 s on sorrow\, spiritual faith and human connection. These are poems that a
 cknowledge life’s difficulties while returning\, again and again\, to af
 fection\, gratitude and delight.\n\nOne poem’s title\, “I’M NOT AS O
 LD AS I USED TO BE\,” offers a fitting introduction to a poet celebratin
 g his 90th birthday with a new book. Elsewhere\, a trip to the laundromat 
 becomes an unexpected encounter with love\, and a walk along the beach bec
 omes a celebration of companionship.\n\nThe gathering combines a literary 
 occasion with a personal milestone: an opportunity to discover Raikes’s 
 poetry and wish its author a happy 90th birthday.
LOCATION:Wonderland Pizzeria
URL:https://wonderlandpizzeria.toast.site/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
