BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:VINES\, VIEWS & VIBES: HARVEST
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
UID:261010AbDqpKWAjkiQY6dwKkN-UA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate **Harvest** in the heart of Sonoma wine country. As 
 gold\, amber\, and crimson foliage sweeps across the valley\, the crisp au
 tumn air comes alive with the sweet\, unmistakable aroma of crush.\n\nFor 
 one special afternoon\, Chef-Vintner **Dustin Valette** opens the doors to
  his Michelin-recognized restaurant\, **The Matheson\,** and its rooftop l
 ounge\, **Roof 106**\, for an extraordinary journey of the senses you won'
 t soon forget.\n\nFramed by vibrant Fall foliage and cozy firepits\, this 
 immersive afternoon pairs extraordinary gastronomy with just released Vale
 tte wines\, and spellbinding live entertainment from rising star **IZZY ES
 COBAR**\, all in support of the **V Foundation for Cancer Research**!\n\n*
 *Your VIP Ticket Includes:**\n\n**Exclusive Valette Wine:** Be among the f
 irst to taste these highly coveted\, brand new releases from Valette Wines
 \, crafted in collaboration with a collective of the world’s most celebr
 ated winemakers.\n\n**Hyper-Seasonal Culinary Pairings:** Taste elevated b
 ites curated by award-winning **Chef-Vintner Dustin Valette**.\n\n**Intima
 te Set by Izzy Escobar:** Experience a rare\, up-close performance by the 
 rising soul-pop sensation - hailed by *Forbes* as **"Your Pop Queen for 20
 26"** - following show-stopping festival appearances at BottleRock\, Austi
 n City Limits\, and the Montreal International Jazz Festival.\n\n**Premier
  Silent Auction:** Bid on rare wines\, exclusive travel\, music\, sports\,
  and culinary experiences\, with 100% of auction proceeds benefiting The V
 's goal of Victory Over Cancer.\n\n**Take Home Wine for a Cause:** Bottles
  of Valette Wines will be available for purchase\, with **20%** of proceed
 s benefiting the V Foundation!\n\n**Reserve Your Spot Today!**\n\nTo prese
 rve an intimate experience\, **tickets are strictly limited and will sell 
 out fast!** Secure your entry now to immerse yourself in the bounty of har
 vest\, experience powerhouse talent up close\, and make a meaningful impac
 t.\n\nThe event benefits the V Foundation for Cancer Research\, who since 
 1993 has funded **over $500 million** in game-changing cancer research gra
 nts.
LOCATION:The Matheson
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/vines-views-vibes-harvest-tickets-2002101
 831473
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sing Napa Valley presents "American Songbook Singer Showcase"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T170000
UID:261008ath0zu5vw0ORjwYm0sMkAw
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate America’s musical heritage with Sing Napa Valley a
 t the American Songbook Singer Showcase. Presented in honor of the United 
 States’ 250th anniversary\, this lively afternoon concert travels from t
 he 1920s through the early 1960s with jazz standards\, Broadway favorites\
 , and memorable songs from film. Two concerts: Saturday\, October 24 & Sun
 day\, October 25 at 3pm.\n\nWhether these classics are lifelong favorites 
 or brand-new discoveries\, American Songbook Singer Showcase promises an u
 plifting celebration of music’s power to bridge generations and bring pe
 ople together.\n\nEnjoy timeless music by George and Ira Gershwin\, Cole P
 orter\, Hoagy Carmichael\, and Irving Berlin\, including favorites such as
  “Mr. Sandman\,” “Honeysuckle Rose\,” “Night and Day\,” and 
 “Dream a Little Dream of Me.” Sing Napa Valley choir members and speci
 al guests will take the spotlight in solos\, duets\, trios\, and small ens
 embles\, joined by collaborative pianist Anthony Mayor. Bring family and f
 riends for an uplifting celebration of music that connects generations.
LOCATION:American Legion Hall
URL:http://www.singnapavalley.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
