BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eric Lindell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T200000
UID:26101263gRAUYyCkuqc-PmKR5n-Q
DESCRIPTION:Born in San Mateo\, California in 1969\, Lindell spent countle
 ss hours in San Francisco\, soaking up the musical sounds of the city\, ev
 entually leading him to pick up first the bass and then the guitar and har
 monica. With a love of music and skateboarding\, Lindell formed a few punk
 y garage bands early on while his musical horizons expanded. He listened t
 o the deep blues of Buddy Guy\, Junior Wells\, Jimmy Reed and Albert King 
 before drifting toward the R&B sounds of The Impressions\, Stevie Wonder a
 nd Donny Hathaway\, soaking up the soul and learning how to craft a song. 
 After performing at bars on the West Coast with a few short-lived bands\, 
 Eric formed his own group in 1993. He quickly gained a loyal Northern Cali
 fornia audience thanks to countless performances and many late-night jam s
 essions. Established stars like Charlie Musselwhite and Tom Waits attended
  his shows\, as did overflow crowds of music fans.\n\nWith music on his mi
 nd\, Lindell headed to New Orleans in 1999\, where he quickly discovered t
 he pulsating and dynamic roots scene. He gravitated toward the West Bank d
 ive bars of Gretna and Algiers\, where he befriended many older area music
 ians who helped him get regular work as a performer. Some of New Orleans' 
 finest players\, including keyboardist Ivan Neville and drummers Harold Br
 own \\(War\\)\, Stanton Moore \\(Galactic\\) and Johnny Vidacovich \\(Prof
 essor Longhair\, Astral Project\\) often joined him on stage. Galactic bas
 sist Rob Mercurio began sitting in as well\, and word of Lindell's immense
  talents quickly spread around the city. Stars like Branford Marsalis\, Th
 e Neville Brothers and John Scofield began showing up at his gigs and embr
 acing this fresh California kid's funky music. According to Lindell\, "It'
 s a great feeling to be recognized for your music in New Orleans." Since 2
 003\, in addition to his own gigs\, Lindell regularly joins forces with Iv
 an Neville\, Moore and Mercurio \\(when time and schedules permit\\) and t
 hey perform to overflow crowds as Dragon Smoke.\n\n2006's Change In The We
 ather delighted and surprised music fans hungry for a truly original artis
 t. Lindell's deceptively simple sounding songs\, laid back grooves and hoo
 k-laden melodies were fueled by guests including Brown\, Neville and Moore
 . Critics across the country went wild\, with reviews and features in Reli
 x\, OffBeat\, Guitar Player\, Down Beat\, The New Yorker\, The New York Pr
 ess and many other national and regional publications. Singer And Musician
  magazine put Eric on the cover and many newspaper entertainment sections 
 did the same.\n\n2007's Low On Cash\, Rich In Love and 2009's Gulf Coast H
 ighway pushed Lindell farther into the spotlight. Appearances on Late Nigh
 t With Conan O'Brien and National Public Radio's Mountain Stage solidified
  his stature as an artist who simply could not be ignored. Many of his son
 gs have appeared in films and television shows\, including Boston Legal an
 d Treme. He has collaborated and shared stages with blues and rock luminar
 ies\, including John Fogerty\, Luther Dickinson and Anson Funderburgh.\n\n
 With Revolution In Your Heart\, Lindell was more than ready to come home t
 o Alligator. "The timing is perfect. I'm so excited to get back to focusin
 g on what I do and have such a great team behind me\," he says. Upon relea
 se of the album\, Lindell and his band will tour heavily\, reuniting with 
 old friends and\, as always\, earning new fans at every stop. AllMusic dec
 lares Lindell a singular talent\, saying\, "He plays soulful\, funk-drench
 ed\, tight and focused grooves. He is a quadruple threat as a solid songwr
 iter\, impressive guitarist\, affecting singer and harmonica blower. This 
 is music that's deceptively difficult to create. Lindell makes it seem not
  just easy\, but natural."
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040464858?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Healthy Hearty Meal Prep with Erin Shallat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T120000
UID:261005FoEAO-5gP0mjjadp7JLLgQ
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, October 5\, 2026 10:00 am to 12:00 pm\n\nWeekly on Mo
 ndays\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nCategory\n\nCulinary Art
 s\, Wellness\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\n
 Registration Cost:\n\n$25\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registrat
 ion Cost:\n\n$25\n\nAs the founder of Erin Shallat Catering in San Francis
 co\, Erin brings over two decades of experience in transforming nutrition 
 into an art form. Her unique approach intertwines advanced studies in nutr
 ition with a deep passion for the culinary arts. Erin’s goal is to make 
 meal prep approachable and not intimidating for everyone\, encouraging stu
 dents to gain confidence in the kitchen. She believes in working with seas
 onal produce and what’s available\, helping students learn to create hea
 lth-conscious yet tantalizing menus that embrace both flavor and wellness.
  Introducing our Fall/Winter Cooking Series—designed for both returning 
 and new students. This six-week program runs Mondays and Wednesdays\, each
  with a unique focus to offer variety\, skill-building\, and fun throughou
 t the season.Every Monday\, students will dive into healthy\, hearty meal 
 prep sessions. Each class focuses on creating nutritious\, satisfying dish
 es that can be portioned out and taken home—perfect for fueling the week
  ahead. These hands-on sessions ensure participants leave with ready-to-ea
 t meals and new confidence in their culinary skills.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/healthy-hearty-meal-prep-wi
 th-erin-shallat/2026-10-05/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T194500
UID:2610018hhhCNZEoE-MSObwUcWYEg
DESCRIPTION:Bring a flashlight and your sense of wonder as you e
 xplore the park after dark. This hike heads up to the summit o
 f Bald Mountain\, where we will see the moon rise over the May
 acamas and the sun set over Sonoma Valley. This is a strenuous
  hike of approximately 6.5 miles with 1500\\+ of vertical and s
 ome steep sections \\(not recommended for children under 12\\).\n\
 nMeet at the main parking lot at least 10 minutes prior to the
  start time. Advance registration is $10 for general admission\,
  or $5 for youth \\(12-17 year olds\\)\, students\, Sugarloaf me
 mbers\, Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers. All minors must be accompani
 ed by a parent or legal guardian. You must register on this pa
 ge to attend\; tickets on site are $15 \\(exact change only\\) an
 d might not be available. Bring your flashlight\, at least 32oz
  of water\, snacks\, and extra layers for the evening. Parking 
 fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/oct2026moon-bald
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T170000
UID:260930e2fLOWrQAkCnW7sZXeq2LA
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two *ofrendas* in the House of Happy Walls Museum from 
 Oct. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tra
 dition that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spa
 nish for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the mem
 ory of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and ad
 venturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected t
 o the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, tradi
 tional elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, 
 the installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing an
 d travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, an
 d the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared
 \, participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\
 , and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\
 , drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a 
 beloved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more pe
 ople participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitor
 s who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or
  even a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hanna Center's 27th Annual Golf Classic
