BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jumpstart Your Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T160000
UID:260629QOVLQ_8BckCM8TtAvZhRDQ
DESCRIPTION:Every person experiences an ebb and flow to the tides of their
  creativity. We will share space together to design\, exchange ideas\, and
  hold ourselves accountable to our unique interests! The first portion of 
 our time together will involve a check-in discussion of ‘what is'\, lead
 ing into ‘what could be'. The talk will be facilitated by Erin Partridge
 \, an art therapist with a long history of supporting people in reengaging
  with creativity. After our initial talk\, we will have some time to indiv
 idually focus on our creative practices in the space of the gallery. Befor
 e we close\, we will share anything that came up in the process. Bring you
 r ideas\, a project\, and an interest in creative community. Please be min
 dful of what you choose to show up with-something quiet\, easy to clean up
 \, and non-disruptive to your fellow creatives. Not sure where to begin? S
 ome basic materials are available\, thanks to a donation from  Blick Art M
 aterials . Open for all ages-youth under 12 with an adult chaperone please
 ! Mondays\, 1-4 PM Facilitator: Erin Partridge
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/jumpstart-your-art/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Endless Inspiration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T180000
UID:261014p2_flX-tzESeqgp8EA1eHw
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  10/12/26\n\nNOVEMBER EXHIBIT: EN
 DLESS INSPIRATION\n\nEXHIBIT DATES – October 26  – November 22\, 2026
 \n\nRECEPTION: SATURDAY\, November 7\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Ron 
 Sumner and Karen Miller and learn about their art and inspiration.  Be su
 re to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful 
 work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma County 
 artist\, Ron Sumner\, presents Endless Inspiration\, a collection of new p
 aintings and classic works that highlight his lifelong love of nature feat
 uring landscapes\, animals and wildlife\, with a special focus on birds. 
  The essence of this golden state shines forth in “California Hills\,”
  a large oil painting of a sweep of oak covered hills.   Turning to wild
 life\, Sumner’s masterful watercolor rendition in the “Young Fox” ca
 ptures its wild nature on stark alert.  And the compelling presence of a 
 most majestic bird is beautifully memorialized in his “Blue Heron” wat
 ercolor.  Other birds depicted in his works include parrots\, penguins an
 d owls.  “In my painting\, I always strive to translate my emotional re
 sponse to the world of nature around us – to share this deep feeling wit
 h those who view my work\,” commented Sumner on his inspiration.\n\nA li
 felong Northern Californian\, Sumner began his art training in school.  A
 fter earning a BFA from the California College of Arts & Crafts\, he was a
  technical illustrator for a number of years before transitioning to a ful
 l-time fine arts painter.  With an emphasis in watercolor\, he has won nu
 merous awards\, including Best of Show at the Society of Western Artists.
   His portrait of John F. Kennedy is part of the permanent collection at 
 the John F. Kennedy Library.  He has exhibited widely and was part of the
  Veterans Art Show for CA vets in 2023.\n\nMeet the artist: Sumner will co
 -host Art Nite on 11/5 from 5 pm to 7 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showc
 ase features Karen Miller’s Historic Gems\, featuring pastel paintings t
 hat honor our history – local artifacts that are disappearing.  Highlig
 hting this exhibit\, “Ghost Bridge\,” an early 20th century railroad b
 ridge known as Healdsburg Railroad Bridge is soon to give way for the Smar
 t Train.  Its unique style is a key element to our local character but sa
 dly could not be upgraded for modern rail.  From old trucks to a beloved 
 schoolhouse\, these paintings harken fond memories.  Part of our world fo
 r years\, they enriched our lives and are not to be forgotten.  Noted Mil
 ler on the impetus for her series\, “I want to catch old things before t
 hey’re gone – memorializing those things close to our hearts.”\n\nMe
 et the artist: Miller will host the Gallery on October 26 and November 2\,
  11\, 14 & 15 from 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\n Also join us for ART NITE HEALDSB
 URG\, Thursday\, November 5\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the
  1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and cr
 eativity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\
 nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\
 \) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    www.upstairsart gallery.net
  \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at b
 vdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit:  Endless Inspiration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T180000
UID:2610138_vZbPQ4t0GXYK8jt4658g
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  10/12/26\n\n**NOVEMBER EXHIBIT: 
 ENDLESS INSPIRATION**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES **– October 26  – November 22\
 , 2026**\n\n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, November 7\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to
  meet Ron Sumner and Karen Miller and learn about their art and inspiratio
 n.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a 
 beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSo
 noma County artist\, **Ron Sumner\,** presents **Endless Inspiration**\, a
  collection of new paintings and classic works that highlight his lifelong
  love of nature featuring landscapes\, animals and wildlife\, with a speci
 al focus on birds.  The essence of this golden state shines forth in “C
 alifornia Hills\,” a large oil painting of a sweep of oak covered hills.
    Turning to wildlife\, Sumner’s masterful watercolor rendition in th
 e “Young Fox” captures its wild nature on stark alert.  And the compe
 lling presence of a most majestic bird is beautifully memorialized in his 
 “Blue Heron” watercolor.  Other birds depicted in his works include p
 arrots\, penguins and owls.  “In my painting\, I always strive to trans
 late my emotional response to the world of nature around us – to share t
 his deep feeling with those who view my work\,” commented Sumner on his 
 inspiration.\n\nA lifelong Northern Californian\, Sumner began his art tra
 ining in school.  After earning a BFA from the California College of Arts
  & Crafts\, he was a technical illustrator for a number of years before tr
 ansitioning to a full-time fine arts painter.  With an emphasis in waterc
 olor\, he has won numerous awards\, including Best of Show at the Society 
 of Western Artists.  His portrait of John F. Kennedy is part of the perma
 nent collection at the John F. Kennedy Library.  He has exhibited widely 
 and was part of the Veterans Art Show for CA vets in 2023.\n\nMeet the art
 ist: Sumner will co-host Art Nite on 11/5 from 5 pm to 7 pm.\n\nThe Stairw
 ay Smallworks Showcase features **Karen Miller’**s **Historic Gems\,** f
 eaturing pastel paintings that honor our history – local artifacts that 
 are disappearing.  Highlighting this exhibit\, “Ghost Bridge\,” an ea
 rly 20th century railroad bridge known as Healdsburg Railroad Bridge is so
 on to give way for the Smart Train.  Its unique style is a key element to
  our local character but sadly could not be upgraded for modern rail.  Fr
 om old trucks to a beloved schoolhouse\, these paintings harken fond memor
 ies.  Part of our world for years\, they enriched our lives and are not t
 o be forgotten.  Noted Miller on the impetus for her series\, “I want t
 o catch old things before they’re gone – memorializing those things cl
 ose to our hearts.”\n\nMeet the artist: Miller will host the Gallery on 
 October 26 and November 2\, 11\, 14 & 15 from 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\n Also j
 oin us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, November 5\, 5 – 7 pm. 
  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a communi
 ty event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participati
 ng.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\,
  Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    
 **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beve
 rly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BellyDancing with Carem
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T190000
UID:261012jT2Lr9-VN0WK4sDk3lG6tg
DESCRIPTION:Bellydancing for Beginners \n\nDiscover the beauty of Raqs Sh
 arqi \\(bellydance\\). This beginner-friendly class introduces you to fou
 ndational bellydance technique\, including hip movements\, isolations\, un
 dulations\, traveling steps\, combinations and musicality. You’ll develo
 p coordination\, body awareness\, strength\, and confidence while learning
  to move with greater ease and expression.\n\nNo previous dance experience
  is required. All bodies and experience levels are welcome.\n\nCome move t
 o the music\, connect with your body\, and discover the joy of bellydancin
 g\n\nCAREM LOVE\n\nCarem Love is a wellness advocate\, professional dancer
 \, and certified yoga instructor with a Bachelor’s degree in Dance. She 
 has extensive training in Bellydance\, a deep passion for Latin dance\, an
 d is certified in Hatha\, Vinyasa\, and Children’s Yoga.\n\nBelly dance 
 has profoundly supported her health\, well-being\, and dance career\, insp
 iring her to help others experience the same body-mind benefits. In her cl
 asses\, students learn to connect more deeply with themselves.\n\nDATE: Mo
 nday\n\nTIME: 6:00 PM\n\nWHERE: Salsa Dance Marin\, 4140 Redwood Hwy 8\, S
 an Rafael
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/belly-dancing-with-carem/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T170000
UID:2610042QJVGyAnl0GHmaKIxynXyQ
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
