 n\nFree entry. Donations greatly appreciated.\n\nConcessions open for purc
 hase.\n\nAssistive listening devices available.\n\n Sponsored by Deanna M
 adeson\n\nIn this noir classic\, detective Sam Spade (Humphrey Bogart) get
 s more than he bargained for when he takes a case brought to him by a beau
 tiful but secretive woman (Mary Astor). As soon as Miss Wonderly shows up\
 , trouble follows as Sam's partner is murdered and Sam is accosted by a ma
 n (Peter Lorre) demanding he locate a valuable statuette. Sam\, entangled 
 in a dangerous web of crime and intrigue\, soon realizes he must find the 
 one thing they all seem to want: the bejeweled Maltese falcon.\n\n Releas
 ed Oct 18\, 1941\n\nCrime\, Drama\n\nRuntime 1h 40m
