BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Drawing Portraits From Photos (3 Session Class)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T210000
UID:261023IwenLUKuiEuas4qI-NCTwA
DESCRIPTION:Introduction to Drawing Portraits from Photos \n\nNovember 4th
 \, 11th\, and 18th \n\n6:00-9:00pm \n\n$150.00 \\+ $15.00 Materials Fee = 
 $165.00 \n\nAge Restricted to 18\\+ \n\nAbout this class: \n\nIn this thre
 e week course\, students will learn and practice observational skills and 
 fundamental drawing techniques while learning the basics of drawing portra
 its from photographs. \n\nDrawing human faces requires the same basic dra
 wing skills that one employs for any subject - observing proportion\, flat
 tening shapes\, and utilizing line or value to convey volume. But the conc
 eptual weight of human faces tends to intimidate artists. When drawing any
  subject\, the hardest skill is simply learning to see\, a skill that anyo
 ne can be taught\, practice\, and hone. This course will focus on the prac
 tice of looking\, and discovering strategies to find objectivity when rend
 ering portraits. \n\nThis class is for anyone who wants to practice and a
 dvance their drawing skills - beginners\, those who haven’t practiced in
  years\, or any artists who just want to learn new techniques and practice
  their skills with consistent feedback and guidance. Through demonstration
 \, practice\, and reflective discussion\, this class will explore the foun
 dations of rendering human expression with classical drawing techniques in
  a low pressure environment. \n\nObservational drawing gives all artists 
 a foundation of practical knowledge and skills that infinitely expands the
  possibilities of what one can create. If your ideas feel limited by your 
 drawing skills\, if you feel frustrated or stuck in your painting practice
 \, or if you simply want to start drawing and are looking for a place to s
 tart\, this is the class for you.\n\nAbout the Instructor: Hannah Day rece
 ived her BA in Visual Arts with an emphasis on drawing and printmaking fro
 m University of San Diego\, then attended University of Hawaii at Manoa to
  receive her MFA in printmaking. Hannah’s etchings have been internation
 ally shown and collected\, but her art practice also includes paper cuttin
 g\, graphite\, and watercolor. She has taught all ages in many mediums. Th
 ese days\, Hannah primarily teaches watercolor\, observational drawing\, a
 nd paper cutting. You can view her work at www.hannahdrawstrees.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classeslectures/p/drawingportraitsfromphotos
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
