DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T210000
UID:261020A1iQ6YubfUuBl1kEn4s0aQ
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to Ride the Cyclone!\n\nFunny\, wildly original\, un
 expectedly moving\, and just a little bit twisted\, Ride the Cyclone is th
 e cult-hit musical that has become a phenomenon with audiences around the 
 world. When six members of a high school choir meet an untimely end in a r
 oller coaster accident\, they awaken in a strange carnival limbo where a m
 ysterious fortune-telling machine offers them an impossible chance: one of
  them can return to life. To decide who deserves the second chance\, each 
 must tell their story in a bizarre\, hilarious\, and heartfelt competition
  unlike anything you’ve seen before.
LOCATION:Novato High School Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/marin-school-of-the-art
 s-presents-ride-the-cyclone-teen-edition/19953644/2026-11-06T19
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Hunting for the Snark Illustrations” with the Jack London Soc
 iety
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T123000
UID:261019G4Q_lE0DMkep9H5lNwnExg
DESCRIPTION:**Step inside the House of Happy Walls Museum for a fascinatin
 g exploration of Jack London’s photographic journey aboard the Snark wit
 h Professor Emerita Any Tucker.**\n\nJack London always referred to *The C
 ruise of the* Snark (1911) as an “illustrated book.” The pictures were
  central to his authorial vision of the voyage to the South Pacific that h
 e and Charmian London embarked on in April of 1907. Maddeningly\, in the p
 rocess of preparing the manuscript of *The Cruise of the* Snark for public
 ation\, Macmillan & Co. made a hash of the author’s design\, misplacing 
 some of the book’s 119 photographs and scrambling the captions Jack so c
 arefully assembled.\n\nTucker explains\, “While Jay Williams\, my co-edi
 tor for Volume 13 of Oxford UP’s ‘*Complete Works of Jack London*\,’
  has been collating various iterations of the essays collected in ‘*The 
 Cruise of the* Snark’ to prepare a definitive copy text\, I’ve been tr
 ying to track down the original photographs for the book.  The treasure h
 unt has proved more challenging—and surprising—than expected. The pict
 ures\, most by Jack with a few by Martin Johnson\, the Snark’s young coo
 k and engineer\, are scattered among far-flung sources—beginning with Ch
 armian London’s huge collection of photo albums at the Huntington Librar
 y and multiple binders of prints and negatives housed in the California St
 ate Parks collection at Sonoma Barracks. My search eventually took me to a
 rchives in Chanute\, Kansas\; Auckland\, NZ\; and the British Museum\, for
  it turns out that there was another\, unacknowledged contributor to Jack
 ’s illustrated book.”\n\n**About the speaker:** Amy Tucker is Professo
 r Emerita of the English Department of Queens College\, CUNY\, where she t
 aught American literature and cultural studies. She has published essays o
 n art\, travel and literature\, and served as guest editor of a volume on 
 Charmian London for “*Women’s Studies: An Inter-Disciplinary Journal.
 ”*  Her books include “*The Illustration of the Master: Henry James a
 nd the Magazine Revolution\;” “Visual Literacy*: *Writing about Art\;
 ”* and\, most recently\, “*I’m Used to Playing Lead: Memoirs by Wome
 n in Jazz\,”* to be brought out by Equinox in January\, 2027. Tucker and
  Williams have received a two-year grant from the National Endowment for t
 he Humanities to work on their volume for “*The Complete Works of Jack L
 ondon*.”\n\n*This event is part of a speaker series co-hosted by Jack Lo
 ndon Park Partners and the Jack London Society\, honoring the 150th annive
 rsary of Jack London’s birth. JLPP is grateful for the support of the Ja
 ck London Society and its scholars in bringing this speaker series to life
 . Join us at Jack London State Historic Park throughout 2026 for a compell
 ing lineup of speakers celebrating Jack London’s legacy.  Learn more at
 * https://jacklondonsociety.org/*.*
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/jl-speaker-series-amy-tucker/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seen.Valued.Supported: A free event for dementia family caregivers
