DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T133000
UID:2610178gwXRACM70ms9-vYtYbf_w
DESCRIPTION:Caring for someone living with dementia? You are seen\, valued
 \, and supported. 💜\n\nIn honor of National Family Caregiver Month\, jo
 in the Alzheimer's Association\, Redwood Caregiver Resource Center\, and C
 ouncil on Aging for a free education event for family caregivers. Learn pr
 actical strategies to create balance\, prevent burnout\, and build realist
 ic routines that support both you and the person in your care.\n\n📅 Fri
 day\, November 6\, 2026 | 11:30 a.m.-1:30 p.m. 📍 Council on Aging\, 30 
 Kawana Springs Rd.\, Santa Rosa 🆓 Free to attend. Optional respite care
  is also free\, but it must be reserved by 11/2 (no walk-ins).\n\nRegister
 : https://tinyurl.com/SEEN2026 Respite requests: Salina Gonzalez\, sgonzal
 ez@councilonaging.com
LOCATION:Council on Aging 
URL:https://tinyurl.com/SEEN2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
