BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ryan MacNeill & The Big Deal & JeConte & Archer Monk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
UID:2610203CXXQ-LGB02D-sriCmVeBg
DESCRIPTION:Experience a full day and night of live music in Point Reyes S
 tation as Ryan MacNeill & The Big Deal and JeConte take over the legendary
  Old Western Saloon on Saturday\, November 7.\n\nRyan MacNeill & The Big D
 eal kick things off from 4:00–7:00pm\, bringing their blend of Cosmic Am
 ericana\, rock & roll\, country\, and psychedelic roots music to one of We
 st Marin’s most iconic stages.\n\nFronted by Ryan MacNeill\, the band pa
 irs traditional songwriting with expansive guitar textures\, rich vocal ha
 rmonies\, driving basslines\, swirling organ\, and dynamic rhythms. Their 
 music moves easily between open-road Americana and exploratory\, psychedel
 ic jams—grounded in the traditions of American roots music while pushing
  well beyond them.\n\nThe evening continues from 8:00–11:00pm with JeCon
 te\, featuring rock & roll harmonica and special guest Archer Monk. The al
 l star band includes Matt Allard on organ\, Jono on bass\, Adam Bowers on 
 slide guitar\, and Andrew Tuckman on drums.\n\nSet in the heart of Point R
 eyes Station\, it’s an afternoon and evening of live music\, good times\
 , and West Marin character at the Old Western Saloon\, brought to you by W
 ild West Ferments.\n\nOld Western Saloon\n\n11201 CA-1\n\nPoint Reyes Stat
 ion\, CA 94956\n\nSaturday. November 7 2026\n\n4:00 – 7:00pm – Ryan Ma
 cNeill & the Big Deal\n\n8:00pm – 11:00pm – JeConte and Friends
LOCATION:Old Western Saloon
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108998370?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Atelier One Open Studios
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T170000
UID:261017xKZXgCB7zk-8yR6Ip8dHfw
DESCRIPTION:On November 7th and 8th\, 2026\, Atelier One artists will cel
 ebrate the buildings’ 39th year as a haven for creativity\, with an ope
 n studio weekend. The historic building nestled in wine country’s villag
 e of Graton was transformed from an abandoned apple processing facility in
 to working studios by visionary architect\, Lamont Langworthy in 1987.  
 You are all invited to this once a year event where artists will demonstra
 te and discuss\, show and offer for sale\, a diverse range of artistic end
 eavors.  Hours will be 11 to 5 each day.  2860 Bowen St. Graton .
LOCATION:Atelier One
URL:http://atelierone.blogspot.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Senderos: Los Wappo en Wilikos
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T104500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T130000
UID:261017Dmb2Cex2CEGABDYDtBGyFg
DESCRIPTION:\\[Translated to English below\\] Aprende acerca de las histor
 ias y tradiciones de la tribu Wappo\, una de las tribus originarias de est
 a área\, en esta caminata familiar de 2 millas. Nos reuniremos en el esta
 cionamiento del granero blanco \\(el White Barn\\) y caminaremos el sender
 o Meadow mientras escuchamos acerca de la historia cultural de los Wappo e
 n una de sus aldeas ancestral\, Wilikos\, hoy en día parte de Sugarloaf.
  \n\nEvento gratuito\; requiere registración. Hay transportación dispon
 ible gratuita dentro de un radio de 20 millas al parque para familias que 
 la necesiten. Para detalles y registración\, visita EVENT LINK\n\nAlterna
 tivamente\, llama a Mario \\(707-387-4087\\)\, Alma \\(707-247-5767\\)\, e
 ntre martes y sábado\\) o escríbenos a senderos@sonomaecologycenter.org.
  ¿No puedes acompañarnos ese día? ¡Guarda la fecha el 5 de diciembre p
 ara más aventuras!\n\nSenderos Naturales es parcialmente respaldado por u
 na beca de Parks California.\n\nFotografía cortesía de Alma Shaw\n\n\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nLearn about the history and traditions of the M
 ishewal Wappo Tribe\, one of the original groups to live in this area. On 
 this family hike\, will walk approximately 2 miles along the Meadow trail 
 while we listen to the cultural history of the Wappo peoples in one of the
 ir ancestral villages called Wilikios\, today found in Sugarloaf.\n\nThis 
 event is planned around a primarily Latino audience and will be conducted 
 in Spanish. Families from underrepresented groups are welcome to join. Fre
 e transportation available within a 20 mile radius of the park for familie
 s in need. For questions\, please email senderos@sonomaecologycenter.org.\
 n\nThis event is partially supported by Route to Parks\, a project of Park
 s California.\n\nPhoto courtesy of Alma Shaw
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/loswappo26
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nancy Fawson Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
UID:261016zEpxY5wpMEOr5UD98tZVHA
DESCRIPTION:Nancy Fawson is a powerhouse Bay Area-based vocalist and songw
 riter whose musical roots run deep in soul\, R&B and rock. Raised on the i
 conic sounds of Sam Cooke\, Etta James\, Aretha Franklin\, Chaka Khan\, St
 evie Wonder\, and Amy Winehouse\, Nancy’s musical influences have left a
 n indelible imprint on her voice and style. With a unique\, soulful tone a
 nd a passion for heartfelt expression\, Nancy connects with her audience o
 n a profound level—delivering each song with purity\, emotion\, and auth
 enticity.\n\nNancy’s vocal range spans across a variety of genres\, incl
 uding soul\, funk\, blues\, R&B\, and rock\, allowing her to bring versati
 lity to every performance. Whether performing with a duo or full band\, sh
 e engages audiences with her compelling stage presence and soulful deliver
 y.\n\nAs the lead singer of the popular Marin-based blues\, soul\, and fun
 k band Corner Pocket\, Nancy continues to captivate crowds with her raw en
 ergy and dedication to the craft. In addition to live performances\, she i
 s also available for recording session work\, offering her talents as both
  a lead and background vocalist.\n\nWith a sound that blends classic influ
 ences with modern flair\, Nancy Fawson is an artist whose voice you won’
 t soon forget.
LOCATION:Murphy's Irish Pub & Restaurant
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109008186?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It's A Grand Night For Singing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T210000
UID:2610168QsbhIrD0U-SafV1bzanwA
DESCRIPTION:Each program features fantastic professional vocalists as well
  as the most promising professional talent of tomorrow. Singers from all o
 ver the San Francisco Bay Area \\(and beyond!\\) perform excerpts from ope
 ra\, musical theatre\, cabaret\, and zarzuela -- a plethora of well-loved 
 musical favorites as well as delightful surprises from the lesser known re
 pertoire. \n\nIT'S A GRAND NIGHT FOR SINGING continues the first Saturday
  of every month at 7pm at the Jarvis Conservatory located at 1711 Main Str
 eet in historic downtown Napa. Tickets are $20 and available at the box of
 fice beginning at 6pm\, with doors opening for General Seating at 6:30pm o
 r you may purchase your tickets early online.
LOCATION:Jarvis Conservatory
URL:https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/iagnfs-november-7th
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
