BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marin Arts & Crafts Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T170000
UID:2610130R0vbzvm6EScKjmR7LDhYA
DESCRIPTION:Marin Arts & Crafts Show returns to the Marin Center Exhibit H
 all November 6–8\, filling the hall with more than 200 exhibits of fine 
 craft\, art and artisan goods. Arriving just as the holiday season gets un
 derway\, the three-day market brings together an exciting mix of artists\,
  artisans and craftspeople for a weekend of art\, handcraft and seasonal d
 iscoveries.\n\nInspired by the Arts & Crafts movement\, the show celebrate
 s craftsmanship\, thoughtful design and artistic expression in its many fo
 rms. Visitors will find jewelry\, ceramics\, textiles\, glass\, woodwork\,
  fine art\, furniture\, wearable art and specialty foods from artisan food
  makers. From hand-dyed silks and sculptural ceramics to finely crafted je
 welry and heirloom-quality woodworking\, the market brings together tradit
 ional techniques\, fresh ideas and contemporary design.\n\nThroughout the 
 weekend\, visitors can talk with artists about their work\, watch demonstr
 ations and explore the many forms of handcraft represented at the show. It
 's a chance to see the details up close\, hear how things are made and get
  to know some of the people behind the work.\n\nThe November show brings a
  festive atmosphere to the Marin Center\, with a bustling marketplace of f
 ine crafts\, art and artisan foods. Visitors can enjoy wine tasting\, samp
 le seasonal treats from specialty food merchants and listen to live music 
 throughout the weekend. Free opportunity drawings offer chances to win won
 derful prizes donated by participating artisans\, adding to the excitement
 .\n\nWith free admission and free parking\, Marin Arts & Crafts Show is an
  inviting way to spend a fall afternoon with family and friends. As the ho
 lidays approach\, the market is also a wonderful place to discover distinc
 tive gifts while supporting independent artisans.\n\n**Marin Arts & Crafts
  Show** November 6–8\, 2026 Friday–Sunday\, 10 a.m.–5 p.m. Marin Cen
 ter Exhibit Hall 20 Avenue of the Flags\, San Rafael\, CA **Free admission
  & free parking**\n\nFor more information\, visit www.MarinArtsAndCraftsSh
 ow.com
LOCATION:Marin Center Exhibit Hall
URL:https://www.artsandcraftsshow.com/marin.php
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Self-Compassion for Shame: Practical Skills for Emotional Wellbein
 g
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T160000
UID:261012mmUOY_heZkGV_xmt-V6GQg
DESCRIPTION:with Christopher Germer and Carolina Bautista-Velez\n\nWhat’
 s wrong with you? Who do you think you are?\n\nAll humans can experience s
 hame—including the most practiced meditators and meditation teachers. It
  can even happen when we’re entirely innocent of wrongdoing\, as well as
  when we make a mistake. Whenever we feel bad about ourselves\, for whatev
 er reason\, there’s usually a touch of shame present. It strikes us at t
 he core of our being and yet has nothing to do with who we really are.\n\n
 The power of shame is largely an illusion. As meditation teacher Tara Brac
 h says\, shame often masquerades as a “trance of unworthiness” that ge
 ts its power from our instinctive avoidance of it. However\, when we look 
 at shame through the eyes of self-compassion\, we can discover something q
 uite surprising—that shame is an innocent emotion arising from a univers
 al wish to be loved. This insight opens the door to compassion and self-un
 derstanding. Research shows that self-compassion is the opposite of shame.
  As self-compassion goes up\, shame goes down.\n\nIn this benefit workshop
 \, Chris Germer and Carolina Bautista-Velez present the practice of Self-C
 ompassion for Shame\, specifically tailored to loosen the grip of shame in
  our own lives. The workshop includes short talks\, exercises\, practices\
 , and discussion. Participants will learn 5-6 simple tools to bring home t
 o use in their daily life.\n\nAll are invited to attend this benefit with 
 the awareness that shame can be a difficult human emotion—and that self-
 compassion itself can be emotionally activating. The workshop may be emoti
 onally challenging\, so some familiarity with practicing self-compassion b
 efore joining this workshop may be helpful.\n\nExperienced self-compassion
  teachers will be available as mentors\, in-person and online\, to provide
  information or emotional support to participants\, as needed.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/self-compassion-for-sh
 ame-practical-skills-for-emotional-wellbeing-cr1b26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
