BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:River Shook
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T190000
UID:260910D2Zl0i_K-0S_-FNNKlDUBQ
DESCRIPTION:River Shook releases their galvanizing self-titled solo debut 
 on June 26.\n\nWith arrow-to-the-heart honesty\, vivid characters\, soarin
 g electric guitar\, and shimmering pedal steel\, Shook's unmistakable voic
 e cuts through darkness like a beam of light. The album carries a sense of
  poise and strength\, urging listeners toward deeper self-reflection and h
 onesty about their lives and choices.\n\nIn spring 2025\, as Sarah Shook &
  the Disarmers neared the end of their decade-long run\, Shook was already
  envisioning a new chapter and writing for their solo debut album. When a 
 strong batch of demos yielded no bites from labels\, Shook pitched an unco
 nventional idea to their lead guitarist and partner\, Blake Tallent: they 
 would co-produce the record on a shoestring budget. After the final Disarm
 ers’ show in June\, the pair immediately began recording in their home s
 tudio\, driven by a renewed passion and a shared creative vision.\n\nThe r
 esult is a bold leap forward in production. Shook describes the process as
  more than evolution. "I had to completely kill my old self\," they explai
 n\, shedding limiting beliefs to fully realize the record’s full potenti
 al. Tallent proves a crucial collaborator\, playing nearly every instrumen
 t on the record and helping shape a sound that feels expansive despite its
  minimal resources. Together\, free from outside influence or contractual 
 pressure\, the pair created something deeply personal and sonically singul
 ar.\n\nAcross the album\, Shook explores love\, distance\, freedom\, and s
 elf-revelation. From the wistful urgency of "Country Angel" to the road-wo
 rn vulnerability of "If We Got A Chance" and the cinematic longing of "Los
 t Without Your Love\," the songs balance heartbreak with defiance. Recorde
 d in a rural North Carolina home studio\, River Shook feels larger than li
 fe–an intimate yet sweeping work that confronts hard truths while remind
 ing listeners of their capacity to change.
LOCATION:Little Saint
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108772442?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T163000
UID:26090910jzG7rAjUKPlCpySsZ-1A
DESCRIPTION:**September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month.** On Monda
 y\, Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person S
 enior Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\,
  CA. The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.
 -4:30 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming nat
 ive artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in
  their art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts.
  The artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, gues
 t curator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·
          Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\
 , cultural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry E
 dward Frank\, *Yurok/Kashaya Pomo*\, who will show paintings and work with
  Legos titled *Mind Prison\,*\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas
  (Nico) Vargas\, *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\, whose art was featured at
  the 55th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carret
 ero\; Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\
 , *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Angelica Smith\, *Manchester Point Arena
  and Yokayo Rancheria*\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\,
  *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaug
 h\; Katie Williams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, *Big Valley P
 omo Tribe*.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
