BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pop-up Workshop: Paper Clay Abstraction with Gabriel John Poucher
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T160000
UID:261023U2JVev5Shk2Xk3pg2XiSfQ
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will explore the unique possibilities of paper c
 lay\, with a focus on process-drive sculpture. We will cover nontraditiona
 l building techniques\, using slip as a decorative material\, and creating
  structure through the use of components. The workshop will feature a lect
 ure explaining the unique materials we’ll be using\, followed by a multi
 -part demo and activities. Participants will be provided with materials an
 d are encouraged to investigate playfully\, with a focus on process over o
 utcomes.This workshop coincides with Gabriel’s Solo Exhibition\, ***Burg
 eon\,*** on view at the Sonoma Community Center from November 7 – 29. Ga
 briel’s work stems from the intersection of ecology and queer identity\,
  and the parallel frameworks they provide for resisting rigid categories\,
  binary distinctions\, and expected outcomes. Burgeon examines the notion 
 that transformation does not require resolution. The work draws inspiratio
 n from natural processes of growth and consumption\, and the way they blur
  the boundaries between organism and environment\, individual and collecti
 ve. Constructing clay forms through an extended process of repetition and 
 accumulation\, pattern and deviation\, Gabriel’s work explores the idea 
 that to be in flux is not to be incomplete.Saturday\, November 14\, 2026 1
 2:00 pm to 4:00 pm\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nCategory\n
 \nCeramics\, Workshops\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n17+\n\
 nRegistration Cost:\n\n$65\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$10\n\nTotal Registration 
 Cost:\n\n$75
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/paper-clay-abstraction/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Our Wild Watershed- Owl Hill Film Screening & Q&A
