DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T184500
UID:261023Eg4jLvnjD0KVRuPQ8Is8EQ
DESCRIPTION:Join the Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation for a special evening
  in our Our Wild Watershed series featuring a screening of Owl Hill\, a 15
 -minute documentary exploring the community of owl box keepers and preserv
 ationists working to support and protect owls in the San Francisco Bay Are
 a\, particularly in Sonoma and Marin counties. The film features Laguna Fo
 undation volunteer Nick Jones\, who helped establish and monitor our Barn 
 Owl box cameras at the Laguna Environmental Center. Following the screenin
 g\, filmmaker Sean Restivo will join Nick and representatives from All Abo
 ut Owls\, a local organization dedicated to owl conservation and environme
 ntal education\, for a conversation and Q&A about the film\, local owl con
 servation\, and the community working to protect these remarkable birds.
LOCATION:Laguna Environmental Center
URL:https://OWWOwls26.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
