BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maynard Lyndon Artist Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T000000
UID:261021A0j-58t_Wky9kU9v9W8ybQ
DESCRIPTION:Exhibition: 10.01 through 11.15 Reception: Thursday\, 10.01 fr
 om 4pm-6pm The Sea Ranch Lodge\n\nPlayful Ways of Seeing Now 85\, Maynard 
 has been ‘drawing+painting’ and ‘inventing+model-making’ since ear
 ly childhood — always encouraged to ‘look+learn+create+share.’ He’
 s been doing so for decades\; his ‘sharing’ has been in the realms of 
 teaching and in developing products for the housewares and furniture indus
 tries\, and designing retail environments\, including galleries and design
  shops\, beginning in 1967 when he opened ColorForm — a small toy shop i
 n Santa Monica\, specializing in hand-made playthings.\n\nAs an artist and
  designer\, color + form reign importantly in Maynard’s mind — in his 
 ‘seeing+sharing’ through creating objects and images\, sometimes ‘pl
 ayfully.’ The artworks in this exhibit — whether his 3D ‘Looking Box
 es’ or his paintings+drawings — are ones he’s made in 2026.
LOCATION:The Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:https://www.thesearanchlodge.com/programming/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artazan Handcraft Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:26102190jKOTgSeU-fbZqh-B66fQ
DESCRIPTION:Artazan Handcraft Market returns to Pasadena November 14–15\
 , bringing together artists\, artisans\, craftspeople and the community fo
 r a weekend celebrating creativity and work made by hand.\n\nInspired by t
 he ideas behind the Arts & Crafts movement\, the handcraft market celebrat
 es creativity\, thoughtful design\, skilled work and the people behind the
  things we bring into our lives. That spirit is reflected in a contemporar
 y and wide-ranging mix of handcraft\, encompassing many different material
 s\, traditions and creative approaches.\n\nHeld at the Pasadena Convention
  Center\, the two-day market will be filled with work from independent art
 ists and artisans across an eclectic mix of mediums. Visitors might discov
 er jewelry and metalsmithing\, ceramics and glass\, crochet and fiber art\
 , woodworking and handcrafted clocks\, painting and mixed media\, wearable
  art\, leatherwork\, home décor\, artisan foods and much more. From time-
 honored skills to unexpected new ideas\, the market reflects the remarkabl
 e variety of what people are creating by hand today.\n\nThe weekend will a
 lso connect with Pasadena’s broader creative community\, bringing togeth
 er local and regional artists\, arts organizations\, educators and visitor
 s. Guests can talk directly with artists\, learn about their materials and
  techniques\, take part in hands-on workshops\, watch demonstrations and e
 njoy live music throughout the weekend.\n\nTaking place at the beginning o
 f the holiday season\, the November market offers an alternative to mass-p
 roduced holiday shopping\, with distinctive gifts\, original art\, artisan
  foods and objects for the home\, while directly supporting independent ar
 tists and small creative businesses.\n\nMore than a place to shop\, Artaza
 n offers an opportunity to see handcraft up close\, discover something une
 xpected and experience the incredible range of things being made by hand t
 oday.\n\n**EVENT DETAILS Artazan Handcraft Market** November 14–15\, 202
 6 Pasadena Convention Center • Pasadena\, California Saturday & Sunday 
 • 10 a.m.–5 p.m.\n\nTickets\, workshops\, exhibitor information and ad
 ditional details are available at **Artazan.com**.
LOCATION:Pasadena Convention Center
URL:https://www.artazan.com/pasadena.php
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jim Lauderdale
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
UID:261020kBWWUaoHz0W9mh3CxXJ0pw
DESCRIPTION:Two-time Grammy-winning singer and master songwriter Jim Laude
 rdale is both a "songwriter's songwriter\," who's written/co-written many 
 modern classics for iconic artists\, as well as an intuitive sideman\, who
 's enhanced the music of a bevy of esteemed musicians. As a solo artist\, 
 since 1986 up until now\, he's created a bodywork spanning 37 albums of im
 aginative roots music\, encompassing all that is today’s musical landsca
 pe. His combination of Country\, Bluegrass\, Soul\, R&B and Rock has helpe
 d to pave the way for the current Americana movement.\n\nFor several decad
 es\, Jim has written songs for and worked with some of the finest artists 
 in traditional and modern music including Ralph Stanley\, Elvis Costello\,
  George Strait\, Buddy Miller\, Lucinda Williams\, John Oates\, Solomon Bu
 rke\, Lee Ann Womack\, Old Crow Medicine Show\, Mary Chapin Carpenter\, Bl
 ake Shelton\, the Dixie Chicks\, Vince Gill\, Patty Loveless\, and Gary Al
 lan among others.\n\nLauderdale co-hosts "The Buddy & Jim Show" weekly rad
 io program on SiriusXM with Buddy Miller. Recently\, the Americana Music A
 ssociation honoured him with the WagonMaster Lifetime Achievement Award. J
 im has certainly earned it\, having released a staggering 37 albums with t
 he latest My Favorite Place out June 21st on Sky Crunch Records 2024. \n\n
 Whether solo or band\, Jim Lauderdale a triple threat performer\, songwrit
 er and musician who is constantly reinventing himself!
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108940639?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
