BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author’s Afternoon with Marlo Faulkner on “The Second Mrs. Lon
 don”
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T153000
UID:261019DGJ3qsFIKUSgmaGdDY7fkw
DESCRIPTION:Step into the world of Charmian Kittredge London with author M
 arlo Faulkner as she presents her book\, “The Second Mrs. London."\n\nA 
 native of Coeur d’Alene\, Idaho\, Marlo Faulkner has led a remarkable an
 d adventurous life\, working as a roadie\, English instructor\, columnist\
 , literary scholar\, and a featured speaker for the Jack London Society. H
 er fascination with Charmian London began during a visit to Jack London St
 ate Historic Park\, where she discovered Charmian’s private apartment. Y
 ears of research\, travel\, and study culminated in her new novel\, “The
  Second Mrs. London\,” bringing to life the extraordinary story of one o
 f Sonoma Valley’s most captivating women.\n\nSet in San Francisco at the
  turn of the 20th century\, the novel tells the story of Charmian\, a bold
  and ambitious woman whose life is forever changed when she meets young wr
 iter Jack London. From a broken picnic date to a devoted partnership as fr
 iend\, confidante\, editor\, and companion. Their story is one of passion\
 , resilience\, and determination.\n\nFaulkner will share details of the re
 markable life of Charmian London\, read excerpts from her book inspired by
  this extraordinary woman\, and sign copies for attendees.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/the-second-mrs-london-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Richard Heinberg: A Celebration of His Life and Legacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:261018JT6xRXhqKkGOOut78Y4VdQ
DESCRIPTION:Author • Musician • Senior Fellow at Post Carbon Institute
  • Environmental Educator • Artist • Husband • Friend\n\nYou are w
 armly invited to join family\, friends\, colleagues\, and admirers from ar
 ound the world on November 15th as we come together to celebrate the extra
 ordinary life and legacy of Richard Heinberg.\n\nA Senior Fellow at Post C
 arbon Institute for nearly 20 years\, Richard was a pioneering voice on re
 silience and the energy crisis. He was the author of fourteen books\, hund
 reds of articles\, and the award-winning monthly Museletter.\n\nRichard wa
 s a skilled writer and speaker who could synthesize complex issues and ide
 as into understandable language. His calm demeanor\, sharp wit\, and inten
 se focus made difficult and daunting facts feel bearable.\n\nRichard was a
  lifelong violinist and guitarist who\, more recently\, took up the piano.
  For decades\, he maintained a devoted\, focused daily practice and played
  in bands\, chamber groups\, duos\, and orchestras throughout his life.\n\
 nBeyond his public work\, those who knew him personally were struck by his
  genuine curiosity. He was always asking questions and truly listening for
  the answers.  \n\nJoin us in Santa Rosa on November 15th for an afternoo
 n of gratitude and celebration for a life so fully and generously lived. R
 ichard’s commemoration will be held from 2:30 to 4:00 pm\, with arrival 
 starting at 2:00 pm and a social hour to follow the program.\n\nSeating is
  limited. Please use the RSVP link on EverLoved to save your spot.
LOCATION:See EverLoved for venue information
URL:https://everloved.com/life-of/richard-heinberg/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
