BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Freestyle Playground Dance Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T193000
UID:26100812MzCS8rPUqhi-TkVNItHg
DESCRIPTION:Freestyle Playground — 4-Week Dance & Movement Series\n\n**E
 xplore. Play. Create. Express.**\n\nReady to discover new ways of moving a
 nd expressing yourself through dance?\n\n**Freestyle Playground** is a pla
 yful\, creative dance class designed to expand your movement vocabulary\, 
 spark your imagination\, and help you discover your own unique movement st
 yle.\n\nThrough guided freestyle exercises\, imaginative movement concepts
 \, musicality\, elements of popping\, rhythm\, and body awareness\, you'll
  explore new ways to move\, experiment\, and create.\n\nEach week\, we'll 
 introduce different movement tools and concepts that you can combine\, bui
 ld upon\, and incorporate into your own dancing.\n\n**This isn't a choreog
 raphy-based class.** It's about exploration\, curiosity\, and the freedom 
 to move without worrying about getting it "right."\n\nWhether you're an ex
 perienced dancer looking for fresh inspiration or someone curious about ex
 ploring movement\, all levels are welcome!\n\nClass Details\n\n📍 **Lagu
 na Lab | Sebastopol\, CA**\n\n📅 **4 Tuesdays: October 27\, November 3\,
  10 & 17**\n\n⏰ **6:30–7:30 PM**\n\n💃 **All levels welcome!**\n\nCo
 me expand your creativity\, discover new movement possibilities\, and expe
 rience the joy of freestyle dance!\n\n**No perfection. Just movement\, mus
 ic\, imagination & PLAY!**
LOCATION:Laguna Lab
URL:https://www.tickettailor.com/events/lagunalab/2417443
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bottega Cellar Series with Stag's Leap Wine Cellars
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T210000
UID:26100697EhnSj5Z06zJzWWTcRmEw
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Bottega on November 17 for an elegant evening featu
 ring Stag’s Leap Wine Cellars\, hosted by Winemaker Marcus Notaro. Stag'
 s Leap Wine Cellars is a legendary Napa Valley estate established by Warre
 n Winiarski in 1970 in the Stags Leap District. Just six years after its f
 ounding\, its 1973 S.L.V. Cabernet Sauvignon stunned the world by besting 
 top Bordeaux wines\, including two First-Growths\, at the 1976 Judgment of
  Paris\, a victory that put California and Napa Valley on the global winem
 aking map. Join longtime winemaker Marcus Notaro as the estate continues i
 ts year-long 50th anniversary celebration of the Judgment of Paris. Guests
  will experience a thoughtfully curated progression of wines showcasing th
 e depth and character of the estate\, from vibrant whites to distinguished
  Napa Valley Cabernet Sauvignon\, paired with a seasonal multi-course menu
  by Bottega Executive Chef Alex Espinoza. Each course is designed to compl
 ement the character and expression of the wines\, bringing together refine
 d flavors\, exceptional ingredients\, and the gracious hospitality that de
 fines Bottega.\n\nPrice is inclusive of tax and gratuity.\n\n6525 Washingt
 on Street Suite A9\, Yountville\, CA 94599\n\n\\(707\\) 945-1050
LOCATION:Bottega Napa Valley
URL:https://www.opentable.com/booking/experiences-availability?rid=25489&r
 estref=25489&experienceId=791062&utm_source=external&utm_medium=referral&u
 tm_campaign=shared
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Aspirations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T180000
UID:2609167VNcrOjpikmARTLv33Rj1w
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  9/15/26\n\n**OCTOBER EXHIBIT: AS
 PIRATIONS**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES **– September 28 – October 25\, 2026**\n\
 n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, October 3\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Laura 
 Roney and Linda Loveland Reid and learn about their art and inspiration. 
  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beau
 tiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Laura Roney\,** unveils **Aspirations**\, a new collect
 ion of paintings in oil\, celebrating the unique differing goals people se
 t during our lives\, challenging us to take bold steps forward.  Of unive
 rsal inspiration**\, Aspiration and Awe** splashes the Milky Way’s starr
 y brilliance across the heavens\, capturing our imagination and hope as wo
 rldly cares are left behind.  Moving from natural forces to human endeavo
 r\, looking toward social change\, **Aspiring to Vote**\, the portrait of 
 a hopeful suffragette\, evokes the dream for a better future.  A lifetime
  goal for many\, the marathon\, **Aspiring for 26.2\,** captures the early
  morning excitement waiting for start times.  “People doing ordinary th
 ings but dreaming larger for the future has been a great inspiration for t
 his series.  I hope folks will be inspired by the boldness of people’s 
 dreams\,” commented Roney on her inspiration for the work.\n\nArt has be
 en a lifelong passion for Roney.  Beginning her art studies at a young ag
 e\, whatever avenue she was pursuing in life\, she continued her artistic 
 endeavors.  After a successful career in microbiology and pharmaceutical 
 research\, a family move to Northern California enabled Roney to focus on 
 her art.  She received her MFA from Academy of Art University\, San Franc
 isco.\n\nMeet the artist: Roney will host the Gallery on September 30 and 
 October 1 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features 
 Linda Loveland Reid’s **Intentional Chaos\,** a collection of exciting m
 ixed-media works that explode with excitement and energy. Random patterns\
 , amorphous shapes and dancing dribbles magically coalesce into bold state
 ments.  Intriguing and compelling\, like interlocking gears\, in **Patter
 ns of Memory** multiple patterns interlock on fields of gold and black.  
 “I love throwing ink\, paint and even coffee onto a blank canvas and cre
 ating through instinct\, gesture and emotion.  Distilling energy into sma
 ller works brings new challenges and some happy surprises\,” noted Reid 
 on her creative process.\n\nMeet the artist: Reid will host the Gallery on
  October 23 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n Also join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG
 **\, Thursday\, October 1\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1
 st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and crea
 tivity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nU
 pstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431
 -4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \
 n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvd
 rio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T163000
UID:260909UuEv9sgLQUqI3nV6oGC3gg
DESCRIPTION:**September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month.** On Monda
 y\, Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person S
 enior Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\,
  CA. The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.
 -4:30 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming nat
 ive artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in
  their art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts.
  The artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, gues
 t curator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·
          Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\
 , cultural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry E
 dward Frank\, *Yurok/Kashaya Pomo*\, who will show paintings and work with
  Legos titled *Mind Prison\,*\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas
  (Nico) Vargas\, *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\, whose art was featured at
  the 55th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carret
 ero\; Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\
 , *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Angelica Smith\, *Manchester Point Arena
  and Yokayo Rancheria*\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\,
  *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaug
 h\; Katie Williams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, *Big Valley P
 omo Tribe*.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Salsa – Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T190000
UID:260705kOc_86EV5U6DlpVhLdjBhA
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner salsa class where no experie
 nce or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have fun!\n
 \nGreat for first timers!\n\nNo dance experience required\n\nNon-marking s
 hoes soles\n\nNo partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed environment is perfect f
 or learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyable. In this class 
 you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame for partner-work and
  simple turn patterns. We organize our curriculum so that the movements ar
 e easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals! No experience is ne
 cessary and no partner is required. Drop-in fee is $20.\n\nTuesdays @ 6:00
 pm – 7:00pm\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway #8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote:
  Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-beginners-tuesdays/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T200000
UID:2607047tBA_dQXL0yUcJ29Vm630Q
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\n**Pre- requisite:**\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach we
 ek\, we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connect
 ion that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go bey
 ond the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate
  patterns and styling\, including:\n\n**Turns and Spins:**\n\nMaster your 
 inside and outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Tos
 s moves.\n\n**Intricate Patterns:**\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, a
 s well as various Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n
 \n**Footwork and Styling:**\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced
  footwork like the Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work 
 on styling with a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.
 \n\nThis class is your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead
 -follow connection\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your sa
 lsa vocabulary. Join us and elevate your dance!\n\n**Details:**\n\nNo part
 ner necessary — rotations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear
  **non-marking shoe soles** to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes e
 arly to warm up and get settled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 7:00 pm – 8:
 00 PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-class-intermediate-tuesday/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
